# Admin host gate (#98): only addresses in ADMIN_ALLOWLIST (space-separated IPs or CIDRs) get
# through; everything else is answered 403 and appears in the access log. The default allows
# loopback only, i.e. nobody from outside. Cloudflare Access is an alternative gate (README) and
# needs the admin hostname proxied, so it is off by default.
(admin_gate) {
	@denied not client_ip {$ADMIN_ALLOWLIST:127.0.0.1/32}
	handle @denied {
		respond "Forbidden" 403
	}
}
